# Fixed 2026-09-29, defect 131's class, given to defect 133's lane. Symptom:
# a declaration whose head's line ends with `{`, its body or its members in
# braces and a `}` on the line after them, cost the `{`'s report and then
# `expected_declaration` again at the `}`; the first line inside the braces
# went with the head's recovery, and the rest reached the top level, each
# line a declaration it is not. Cause: inside braces the lexer makes no
# indent, so the body the author wrote was no block the grammar could find,
# and the `}` stood at the margin like a declaration. The habit is now read
# whole, `{` to `}` (`parse/braces.hero`): under a `function`, a `constant`
# or a `test` the `{` is the missing body it stands for, in the block
# reader's words, and the statements inside are read, their own mistakes
# too; under a `record`, a `variant` or an `extern` group the `{` is the
# head's junk, with where the members go, and the braced region goes whole.
# The `}` is the habit's debris and costs nothing. A `{` that is not the
# last thing on its line is no habit, and a `{` on the line below its head
# is not read as one.
# Corrected 2026-09-29 by lane X1 (defect 131's class): a `{` alone on the
# line below its head is read as the habit too, and so is one under a head
# inside a body, `if x == 1 {`, by the block reader under every head, as in
# `fixedbugs-131-a-brace-on-the-line-below-its-head` and
# `fixedbugs-131-a-brace-habit-nested-in-a-body`.

constant LIMIT: i64 {  #~ missing_body
    5
}

test "adds" {  #~ missing_body
    assert 1 + 1 == 2
}

record Point {  #~ expected_end_of_line
    x: i64,
    y: i64,
}

variant Color {  #~ expected_end_of_line
    red,
    green
}

extern "math.h" {  #~ expected_end_of_line
    function sqrt(x: f64) -> f64
}

function first() {  #~ missing_body
    x = 1
    print(x +)  #~ expected_expression
}

function main() {  #~ missing_body
    print(LIMIT)
}

# Corrected 2026-09-29 by lane X4 (defect 130's class, lane X1's finding 1):
# under a `record`, a `variant` or an `extern` group the braced region no
# longer goes whole, as the header says; the `{` is still the head's one
# report, and the members inside are read, their own mistakes told
# (`fixedbugs-130-members-in-braces-are-read`). The members here have none,
# so this case reads the same.
